<title>USA: U.S. denies it asked Saudis to boost oil output.</title>
<headline>U.S. denies it asked Saudis to boost oil output.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Clinton administration said on Monday it had not asked Saudi Arabia or other oil producers to increase their oil output to make up for oil sales from Iraq which had been delayed by the United Nations.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't manipulate oil markets,&quot; a State Department official said.</p>
<p>&quot;We have not asked the Saudis (to increase oil production) and we don't ask them this sort of thing,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The official was denying a news wire report that said Washington had asked the kingdom to boost its oil production after the planned Iraqi oil sales, approved by the United Nations, were held up because of tension in northern Iraq.</p>
